Instead of having it as an option to be set how about asking the player
upon startup for their alignment of preferance but only for select characters.
For example, upon playing a wizard you could choose your alignment and
then begin play.  Also to make this not necessarily a given, make it a 2/3
chance of getting your chosen alignment with a default should you decline
to choose.

Example,

Shall I pick a character for you? [Y, N, or Q(quit)]N

What kind of character are you:

        An Archeologist, a Barbarian.....
        [A,B,C,E,H,K,P,R,S,T,V,W, or Q]W

What alignment do you choose:

        Lawfull, Neutral, or Chaotic.
        [L,N,C, or D(decline to choose)]C

For this game you will be a Lawfull Wizard.


....or....

What alignment do you choose:

        Lawfull, Neutral, or Chaotic.
        [L,N,C, or D(decline to choose)]D

For this game you will be a Neutral Wizard.

I think perhaps only wizards, priests, elves and tourists should be able to
choose.

How about making the healing spell sensitive to alignment and ask you for a
direction when you cast it.  If you are standing by a lawfull monster and
you are chaotic you could cast the heal spell at the monster and do damage
because of opposite alignments.  The same if you were lawfull and attacking
a chaotic monster. Cast at yourself it would have the usual effects and no      effect on neutral monsters.

